{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/485358-mekhet-bane-how-it-works","id":485358,"title":"Mekhet bane: how it works?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-19T06:02:19-07:00","id":485358,"title":"Mekhet bane: how it works?","content":"In core rulebook how the clan Banes works is pretty clear to me except for the Mekhet bane: maybe it's because my english is poor, but I really don't get how it works.<br /> Please, someone can explain it to me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T06:26:48-07:00","id":485380,"title":"","content":"Normally, when Kindred lose Humanity, they may opt to gain a Bane, listed on page 106. This effectively rewrites what a Humanity breaking point would be. Vampires can normally do this three times.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mehket automatically get one of these Banes at Humanity 6, with no change to the Humanity sins. You hit Humanity 6, you go to page 106-107, and pick a bane listed there of your choice. You can also do the rewrite-breaking-point option twice instead of three times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T07:39:05-07:00","id":485401,"title":"","content":"Thanks to my poor english I'm having hard time to understand that bane thing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> you're saying that others clan can choose if they want to gain a bane and become immune to &quot;Killing innocents&quot; sin while for a Mekhet, the bane is mandatory and don't makes him immune on that sin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T07:43:54-07:00","id":485403,"title":"","content":"That sounds about right. <br /> <br /> Of course, the bane is technically a separate thing so I think you could take a breaking point immunity bane along side it, netting two banes at once. Fun times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T08:13:39-07:00","id":485420,"title":"","content":"May I ask what your native language is? Perhaps we have someone here capable of that language to explain it in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T08:56:02-07:00","id":485437,"title":"","content":"I'm italian...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T10:20:38-07:00","id":485477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/485358-mekhet-bane-how-it-works?p=485401#post485401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks to my poor english I'm having hard time to understand that bane thing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> you're saying that others clan can choose if they want to gain a bane and become immune to &amp;quot;Killing innocents&amp;quot; sin while for a Mekhet, the bane is mandatory and don't makes him immune on that sin?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, yes.<br /> <br /> Any time a vampire character experiences a Breaking Point, such as &quot;killing innocents&quot;, they can chose to take one of the Banes from pages 106-107 as an additional weakness. If they do, that act is no longer a Breaking Point for that character. However, from then on the player rolls one fewer die on all rolls to resist detatchment. A character can do this up to three times.<br /> <br /> When a Mekhet character first drops to Humanity 6, they gain one of these weaknesses automatically, but do not become immune to a Breaking Point. This does still count towards their maximum of 3 Banes, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T10:29:43-07:00","id":485485,"title":"","content":"Do they also not get the -1?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T10:42:03-07:00","id":485493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/485358-mekhet-bane-how-it-works?p=485485#post485485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do they also not get the -1?</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>think</i> they still get the -1, but that might be a question for the FAQ.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T11:55:18-07:00","id":485529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/485358-mekhet-bane-how-it-works?p=485493#post485493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>think</i> they still get the -1, but that might be a question for the FAQ.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It has been there a good while, and it does not give the -1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T05:12:17-07:00","id":486238,"title":"","content":"Ok I guess I'm starting to understand anyway the bane is optional? A player can choose to gain a bane or even try luck with a detachment roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T06:02:21-07:00","id":486274,"title":"","content":"They can try their luck on <i>further</i> detachment rolls. The first one needs to be failed to get the option of getting a bane at all. <br /> <br /> You can't become accustomed to murdering people without murdering people at least once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T07:05:35-07:00","id":486307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/485358-mekhet-bane-how-it-works?p=486238#post486238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok I guess I'm starting to understand anyway the bane is optional? A player can choose to gain a bane or even try luck with a detachment roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>Normally, can chose to take a Bane or not any time you fail a Detatchment roll. Either way, you still lose the Humanity this time, but you can optionally chose to gain a Bane and never have to roll Detatchment for that same action again and take a penalty on all other Detatchment rolls.<br /> <br /> For Mekhet, the Bane they get when they drop to Humanity 6 is not optional. They have to take a Bane because of their clan weakness, and they do not gain immunity to a Breaking Point or the penalty to future Detachment rolls for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T07:52:13-07:00","id":486370,"title":"","content":"Not to derail or anything, but if you raise your Humanity from 7 to 8 early on, and keep it alternating between the two numbers (spending Experiences each and every time you drop to 7 to raise it back up to 8), <u>do you NOT get any clan Bane at all, since you technically never dropped to 6 ?</u><br /> <br /> That would technically allow you to bypass the Mekhet Clan Bane + other Bane thingy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T08:50:44-07:00","id":486435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not to derail or anything, but if you raise your Humanity from 7 to 8 early on, and keep it alternating between the two numbers (spending Experiences each and every time you drop to 7 to raise it back up to 8), <u>do you NOT get any clan Bane at all, since you technically never dropped to 6 ?</u> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That would technically allow you to bypass the Mekhet Clan Bane + other Bane thingy? </div> </div> </div>That allow one to &quot;bypass&quot; all Clan Banes as none of them are in effect before you drop to Humanity 6 but after that they are always in effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T09:10:31-07:00","id":486445,"title":"","content":"Although that does raise another question: What happens if a mekhet keeps their humanity high but uses up all 3 bane slots, and <i>then</i> finally drops to 6 for the first time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T10:08:18-07:00","id":486485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/485358-mekhet-bane-how-it-works?p=486445#post486445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although that does raise another question: What happens if a mekhet keeps their humanity high but uses up all 3 bane slots, and <i>then</i> finally drops to 6 for the first time?</div> </div> </div> </div>They'd have 3 Banes eliminating 3 Breaking Points, a -3 on Detatchment rolls, and treat their Humanity as 1 dot lower for the purposes of Humanity-based Banes, including Fire and Sunlight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T10:32:05-07:00","id":486496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/485358-mekhet-bane-how-it-works?p=486445#post486445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although that does raise another question: What happens if a mekhet keeps their humanity high but uses up all 3 bane slots, and <i>then</i> finally drops to 6 for the first time?</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd put a fourth bane on anyways.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T01:49:53-07:00","id":487097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/485358-mekhet-bane-how-it-works?p=486496#post486496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'd put a fourth bane on anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wouldn't allow a Mekhet to take a third bane in the first place, saying it's reserved for your clan bane <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Tho, this is so unlikely to happen in reality, since really.. someone increased his humanity 3 times just to avoid the clan bane?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T03:05:18-07:00","id":487137,"title":"","content":"Maybe they really like the sun or something. I dunno.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T03:37:53-07:00","id":487144,"title":"","content":"I'd let them use up their three bane slots since they'd necessarily have to take banes affiliated with things like seeing people eat to keep their rating at 8+ in the first place. The mechanics of touchstones also don't apply until they're dropping from 7 in accordance with their placement so their rolls suffer from no touchstones until that point also. Or 2, slide their touchstone chart up to accommodate the new humanity floor of their starting Humanity rating being 8+ instead of 7. Congratulations, in your attempt to rules lawyer your way out of your clan bane, you picked up another clan's bane as well. But if they're actually playing to maintain a high humanity then they actually benefit from the touchstone shift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 04-21-2015, 06:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T04:19:08-07:00","id":487182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/485358-mekhet-bane-how-it-works?p=487144#post487144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd let them use up their three bane slots since they'd necessarily have to take banes affiliated with things like seeing people eat to keep their rating at 8+ in the first place. <b>The mechanics of touchstones also don't apply until they're dropping from 7 in accordance with their placement so their rolls suffer from no touchstones until that point also.</b> Or 2, slide their touchstone chart up to accommodate the new humanity floor of their starting Humanity rating being 8+ instead of 7. Congratulations, in your attempt to rules lawyer your way out of your clan bane, you picked up another clan's bane as well. But if they're actually playing to maintain a high humanity then they actually benefit from the touchstone shift.</div> </div> </div> </div>The bolded part is false. As long as you have touchstones at, OR below your current humanity level, you benefit from them.<br /> <br /> Technically, even those above give some benefit (prevent you from getting a -2 penalty for having no touchstones. Detached touchstone (above your humanity) &gt; No touchstone (Dead)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T05:26:52-07:00","id":487196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/485358-mekhet-bane-how-it-works?p=487182#post487182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bolded part is false. As long as you have touchstones at, OR below your current humanity level, you benefit from them.</div> </div> </div> </div>God, thanks for clearing that out. I tried to get a confirmation by re-reading all the sections talking about Touchstones, to no avail. So basically, if I understand correctly, if you are at Humanity 8, and you have a Touchstone attached to Humanity 6 <i>and </i>5 (with the Touchstone merit at rank 1), you would get a +3 dice bonus in your detachment pool and would roll 7 dice for a Humanity 7-8 Breaking Point ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T05:58:57-07:00","id":487210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/485358-mekhet-bane-how-it-works?p=487196#post487196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> God, thanks for clearing that out. I tried to get a confirmation by re-reading all the sections talking about Touchstones, to no avail. So basically, if I understand correctly, if you are at Humanity 8, and you have a Touchstone attached to Humanity 6 <i>and </i>5 (with the Touchstone merit at rank 1), you would get a +3 dice bonus in your detachment pool and would roll 7 dice for a Humanity 7-8 Breaking Point ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, that's correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T19:45:42-07:00","id":487873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/485358-mekhet-bane-how-it-works?p=486445#post486445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although that does raise another question: What happens if a mekhet keeps their humanity high but uses up all 3 bane slots, and <i>then</i> finally drops to 6 for the first time?</div> </div> </div> </div>You slap the ST for allowing something so dumb would be my guess. It is <i>supposed</i> to work by the player commits a sin and takes a bane so that sin is no longer a breaking point. Either the sins would quickly become irrelevant as they would be so high up the chart or the player is behaving out of character. The bane's sin should err on the side of caution and be more or less in line with the current Humanity of the player, so it would not jump straight to mass murder unless the vampire was already of low Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}